### =========================================================================
### MSS301 Summer 2026 Practical Exam - API Test Suite
### Base URL: http://localhost:8080 (HotelGateway entry point)
### =========================================================================

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@roomService = http://localhost:8081
@reservationService = http://localhost:8082

### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. GATEWAY & SWAGGER CONFIG
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Swagger Config Aggregation on Gateway
GET {{gateway}}/v3/api-docs/swagger-config

### 1.2 Preflight CORS OPTIONS for Rooms
OPTIONS {{gateway}}/api/rooms
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type

### 1.3 Preflight CORS OPTIONS for Reservations
OPTIONS {{gateway}}/api/reservations
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Content-Type


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. ROOM SERVICE (Via Gateway port 8080)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Get Rooms list with pagination (Default page=0, size=10)
GET {{gateway}}/api/rooms?page=0&size=10

### 2.2 Filter Rooms by roomType and status
GET {{gateway}}/api/rooms?roomType=SINGLE&status=AVAILABLE

### 2.3 Get Room by ID (Success - HTTP 200)
GET {{gateway}}/api/rooms/1

### 2.4 Get Room by ID (Not Found - HTTP 404)
GET {{gateway}}/api/rooms/999

### 2.5 Create new Room (Success - HTTP 201, default status AVAILABLE)
POST {{gateway}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomNumber": "701",
  "roomType": "SUITE",
  "pricePerNight": 175.00,
  "capacity": 4,
  "floor": 7
}

### 2.6 Create Room with Duplicate roomNumber (HTTP 226 / status 3)
POST {{gateway}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomNumber": "101",
  "roomType": "SINGLE",
  "pricePerNight": 100.00,
  "capacity": 1,
  "floor": 1
}

### 2.7 Create Room with Validation Failure (HTTP 406 / status 2)
POST {{gateway}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomNumber": "702",
  "roomType": "INVALID_TYPE",
  "pricePerNight": -20.00,
  "capacity": 15,
  "floor": 0
}

### 2.8 Partial update Room price (HTTP 200 / status 1)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/rooms/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pricePerNight": 70.00
}

### 2.9 Partial update Room with duplicate roomNumber (HTTP 226 / status 3)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/rooms/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomNumber": "102"
}

### 2.10 Soft delete Room (Set status to MAINTENANCE - HTTP 200 / status 1)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/rooms/1


### -------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. RESERVATION SERVICE (Via Gateway port 8080)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Get Reservations list (Page 0, Size 10)
GET {{gateway}}/api/reservations?page=0&size=10

### 3.2 Filter Reservations by guestName (Partial match)
GET {{gateway}}/api/reservations?guestName=Vinh

### 3.3 Filter Reservations by status
GET {{gateway}}/api/reservations?status=CONFIRMED

### 3.4 Get Reservation Detail by ID (With nested RoomDTO - HTTP 200)
GET {{gateway}}/api/reservations/3

### 3.5 Create Reservation (Success - HTTP 201, auto totalAmount = price x nights)
POST {{gateway}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guestName": "Le Quang Vinh",
  "guestEmail": "vinh@example.com",
  "guestPhone": "0901234567",
  "checkInDate": "20/12/2026",
  "checkOutDate": "23/12/2026",
  "numberOfGuests": 2,
  "roomId": 2
}

### 3.6 Create Reservation with checkOutDate <= checkInDate (HTTP 406 / status 2)
POST {{gateway}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guestName": "Test Error Dates",
  "guestEmail": "test@example.com",
  "guestPhone": "0900000000",
  "checkInDate": "25/12/2026",
  "checkOutDate": "20/12/2026",
  "numberOfGuests": 1,
  "roomId": 2
}

### 3.7 Create Reservation with non-existent roomId (HTTP 404 / status 4)
POST {{gateway}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guestName": "Test NonExistent Room",
  "guestEmail": "test@example.com",
  "guestPhone": "0900000000",
  "checkInDate": "20/12/2026",
  "checkOutDate": "23/12/2026",
  "numberOfGuests": 1,
  "roomId": 999
}

### 3.8 Create Reservation for room in MAINTENANCE (HTTP 400 / status 5)
POST {{gateway}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guestName": "Test Maint Room",
  "guestEmail": "test@example.com",
  "guestPhone": "0900000000",
  "checkInDate": "20/12/2026",
  "checkOutDate": "23/12/2026",
  "numberOfGuests": 1,
  "roomId": 4
}

### 3.9 Create Reservation with numberOfGuests > capacity (HTTP 406 / status 2)
POST {{gateway}}/api/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "guestName": "Test Over Capacity",
  "guestEmail": "test@example.com",
  "guestPhone": "0900000000",
  "checkInDate": "20/12/2026",
  "checkOutDate": "23/12/2026",
  "numberOfGuests": 6,
  "roomId": 2
}

### 3.10 Partial update Reservation dates & recalculate amount (HTTP 200 / status 1)
PUT {{gateway}}/api/reservations/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "checkOutDate": "24/11/2026"
}

### 3.11 Soft cancel Reservation (Set status to CANCELLED - HTTP 200 / status 1)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/reservations/3
